2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T12:38:29-07:00","id":1121460,"title":"","content":"I would happily commit a ritual sacrifice if it meant that Arthurian werewolves would be possible! If I was them though I would not announce the line until post funding to prevent those of us that are disappointed from bailing. Not the nicest way to say it but it the practical course of action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T12:44:24-07:00","id":1121464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1121460#post1121460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would happily commit a ritual sacrifice if it meant that Arthurian werewolves would be possible! If I was them though I would not announce the line until post funding to prevent those of us that are disappointed from bailing. Not the nicest way to say it but it the practical course of action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, more likely and more charitably, they are waiting to see what other stretch goals get funded so that they can balance out the eras each gameline gets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T12:45:06-07:00","id":1121465,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, they may want to wait and see how the Kickstarter ends up, with how many Eras they have and which splats would be chosen, in order to create a more fair division of Eras (so you won;t have, like 5 Changelings and 0 Hunters, for example)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T12:47:03-07:00","id":1121468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1121460#post1121460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would happily commit a ritual sacrifice if it meant that Arthurian werewolves would be possible! If I was them though I would not announce the line until post funding to prevent those of us that are disappointed from bailing. Not the nicest way to say it but it the practical course of action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arthurian era strikes me as Mage/Changeling, because Merlin is an archetypal Wizard and a canon Archmaster in Mage books and references apparently exist in Changeling as well.<br /> <br /> However, if it wins, the Greco-Persian wars era seems to me as rather fitting for Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:38:33-07:00","id":1121494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1121464#post1121464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or, more likely and more charitably, they are waiting to see what other stretch goals get funded so that they can balance out the eras each gameline gets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh do not misunderstand it as a derogatory statement, I have little love for people who offer funds and then abandon ship because they lost the vote. It is merely practical to keep some people from jumping to conclusions and pulling out which as I said is a good if not perhaps kind tactic.<br /> <br /> In any case we only have eight days so I'm not ready counting eras before they batch so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 07-27-2017, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:57:05-07:00","id":1121513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1121468#post1121468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arthurian era strikes me as Mage/Changeling, because Merlin is an archetypal Wizard and a canon Archmaster in Mage books and references apparently exist in Changeling as well.<br /> <br /> However, if it wins, the Greco-Persian wars era seems to me as rather fitting for Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, this and this! I need my (Were)Wolf worshiping Spartans - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1003591-lycos-agema-vigilant-times-to-the-strongest\">like those</a>! Or let just <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> to send his fan Compact for Hunter then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:19:37-07:00","id":1121536,"title":"","content":"I am particularly interested in this era as i am actually currently running a Mage game in a semi-realistic version of Celtic Britain based on a combination of the Runequest supplement Mythic Britain and Keltia a game from Cubicle &amp; (although i think they may just have lost the licence from the original French company that owns the game). Both these games set Arthur and Merlin in a historical setting of dark ages Britain after the retreat of Rome from Britain with Arthur as one of many vying for the rule of the fractious British Celtic tribes and against the background of Saxon invasion and conflicts between the old druid way and the new faith of Christianity. Lots of great politics and intrigue as well as the supernatural backdrop of mythic Celtic Britain. <br /> <br /> So In my setting I have the players as mages working with Merlin (of course a mage!) to support Arthur's claim to rule Britain so i would obviously like to see mage as one of the game lines treated here. I think with this being Celtic Britain the other game line should be (perhaps has to be) Changeling, weaving all the Fae themes into the fight between the old and new faith with teh Celts of the old faith connected strongly to the fae and Changelings. I could also see Werewolf having a lot of relevance with old celtic faith being very ties to connection with the spirit world and spirits of Britain. I could see vampires in there somewhere (maybe Morgana becomes a vampire!) but not as a main line for the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T17:22:06-07:00","id":1121627,"title":"","content":"Yeah; I don't have a strong opinion on what the second gameline should be (my preference for Changeling isn't a particularly strong one); but the first gameline really ought to be Mage. And if it is, Merlin should not appear \u2014 not directly. <br /> <br /> Merlin should be an Ascended Being, having already altered reality to cement the essence of Camelot into reality. The sudden explosion of potential Arthurs that Arcanist refers to is the result of Arthur-flavored Supernal Symbology getting woven into the fabric of reality around this time. And the Camelot that Merlin helped Arthur build as part of Merlin's road to Ascension was considerably closer to the version of Camelot that wyrdhamster was asking about \u2014 meaning that there should be anachronistic Ruins resembling the Romantic Arthur that the \u201creal\u201d Arthur and his men can stumble across. <br /> <br /> Merlin might send an Ochemata (sp?) to aid the Arthur-counterpart of this iteration of reality; but that's as close as you get to the actual Merlin showing up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T21:44:45-07:00","id":1121710,"title":"","content":"Well, I would make slight alteration to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> idea - Merlin is not already Ascended. He is still plotting Archmage that is choosing one of PCs to become his 'Arthur'. Or PCs are trying to stop 'kingdoms destroying Acanthus' - remember, PCs need to DO something in each particular Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-28-2017, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T03:08:20-07:00","id":1121763,"title":"","content":"I support that idea. Not to have something for the PCs to do (that would just be one of several story ideas that need to be written anyway) but because I'd like to see what the Acanthus Awakening is like before Merlin's Ascension changed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T03:17:24-07:00","id":1121764,"title":"","content":"But that wouldn't be a Dark Era; it would be a Mage Shard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T07:22:25-07:00","id":1121831,"title":"","content":"I'm going break with most speculation and say I believe it will be a Changeling/Hunter era, because Mage already has Age of Piracy.<br /> <br /> But I do believe the original Archmage Merlin will be meantioned, but that the current Merlin will be a Changeling, maybe witchtooth kith, with the Lady of the Lake his former Keeper.<br /> <br /> And the Knights of the Round table a Hunter Conspiracy or Compact.<br /> <br /> Alternatively Merlin could be the True Fae and Authur could be a Fairest Changeling with the Crown and Sword Regalia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T07:55:42-07:00","id":1121846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1121831#post1121831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going break with most speculation and say I believe it will be a Changeling/Hunter era, because Mage already has Age of Piracy.<br /> <br /> But I do believe the original Archmage Merlin will be meantioned, but that the current Merlin will be a Changeling, maybe witchtooth kith, with the Lady of the Lake his former Keeper.<br /> <br /> And the Knights of the Round table a Hunter Conspiracy or Compact.<br /> <br /> Alternatively Merlin could be the True Fae and Authur could be a Fairest Changeling with the Crown and Sword Regalia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that when someone says &quot;Mage&quot; or &quot;Wizard&quot; and pretty much every layman immediately thinks of Merlin, as well as the sheer amount of references in Mage books to him, his still existing Legacy and his works, not doing Mage Arthurian would almost be a travesty. It's <i>the</i> Mage era, more than any other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T08:38:21-07:00","id":1121872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1121846#post1121846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that when someone says &quot;Mage&quot; or &quot;Wizard&quot; and pretty much every layman immediately thinks of Merlin, as well as the sheer amount of references in Mage books to him, his still existing Legacy and his works, not doing Mage Arthurian would almost be a travesty. It's <i>the</i> Mage era, more than any other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point and personally would like to see it as mage BUT there is no reason not to subvert those expectations and actually quite a few good arguments to do so. There are lots of options for seeing Merlin and/or Arthur as getting their power from very different sources. Some Arthurian/Merlin literature and film/TV link Merlin to the Fae (e.g. the Merlin mini series that sees his magic as being from the fae who are fighting for the Old Ways) and that would work pretty well. Or Merlin, Arthur and their &quot;knights&quot; are all Werewolves and that is the source of their power. Or to completely subvert the expectations how about Merlin as a Vampire and the whole endeavor of uniting the warring tribes of Britain and fighting against the Saxons is all part of the machinations for power by a Merlin as a powerful Vampire, maybe against his rival for power, morgana. And as Omegaphallic says Hunter would also be an interesting option with Arthur and his followers being a Hunter Conspiracy fighting against the evils of Saxon invaders who are in thrall to infernal powers. <br /> <br /> Actually I may have just managed to argue against my own initial idea of having it as a mage era and think it might be better if it were a Changleing or Werewolf era!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T08:39:35-07:00","id":1121874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1121831#post1121831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going break with most speculation and say I believe it will be a Changeling/Hunter era, because Mage already has Age of Piracy.<br /> <br /> But I do believe the original Archmage Merlin will be meantioned, but that the current Merlin will be a Changeling, maybe witchtooth kith, with the Lady of the Lake his former Keeper.<br /> <br /> And the Knights of the Round table a Hunter Conspiracy or Compact.<br /> <br /> Alternatively Merlin could be the True Fae and Authur could be a Fairest Changeling with the Crown and Sword Regalia.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They'll have to balance the splats, but considering Dave's already weighed-in on this very thread and expressed dismay that they could make Merlin anything but what he's been stated as in many, many sources? I think we're getting Merlin-as-mage. Most likely we're getting a mage and X focused DE, as well, because if you're going to have Merlin around, you'd like to interact with him as a peer, no? (Or, as close as you can anyway.)<br /> <br /> There's a lot to be considered for the second splat, however. I could even see Hunter, with the Knights of the Round Table as a conspiracy of sorts. Adventuring around and slaying things was pretty much all they did, after all!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T08:46:00-07:00","id":1121881,"title":"","content":"Nothing precludes Merlin being a Mage and this era NOT being a Mage era. Matthew already explicitly stated that the Brothers of Ypres are showing up in the Western Front Era. If vampires can appear in the Werewolf/Geist era, what stops Merlin being a Mage here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:04:53-07:00","id":1121889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1121881#post1121881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing precludes Merlin being a Mage and this era NOT being a Mage era. Matthew already explicitly stated that the Brothers of Ypres are showing up in the Western Front Era. If vampires can appear in the Werewolf/Geist era, what stops Merlin being a Mage here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Western front isn't inextricably tied to magic and wizards like Merlin and Morgana. Arthurian stories are magical in their nature, World War isn't. Nor would anyone immediately connect World War or Arthurian era with vampires or even werewolves. The only other splat alongside Mage that has this close connection to Arthurian stories is Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:58:34-07:00","id":1121922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1121881#post1121881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing precludes Merlin being a Mage and this era NOT being a Mage era. Matthew already explicitly stated that the Brothers of Ypres are showing up in the Western Front Era. If vampires can appear in the Werewolf/Geist era, what stops Merlin being a Mage here?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We have <i>literally</i> a few dozen<b> Mage</b> line story hooks across with Merlin being Acanthus pre- or post-Archmastery - it would be like a bit pouring out those hooks to not be used in literal times of Merlin. I'm fairly certain it will be Mage Dark Era - question is rather would it be other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T10:07:37-07:00","id":1121927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1121922#post1121922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We have <i>literally</i> a few dozen<b> Mage</b> line story hooks across with Merlin being Acanthus pre- or post-Archmastery - it would be like a bit pouring out those hooks to not be used in literal times of Merlin. I'm fairly certain it will be Mage Dark Era - question is rather would it be other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it would be leaving those hooks in place for people to use they want and build brand new hooks for two other gamelines that can work alongside them.<br /> <br /> Look, I'm not disagreeing that it probably will be Mage or saying that I don't want it to be. I'm just saying that there are other options and that nothing is a given at this point. I can see Arthurian Eras that are Mummy/Vampire, Werewolf/Changeling, Promethean/Hunter, Demon/Beast, and more variations that could be successful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T10:17:55-07:00","id":1121936,"title":"","content":"As to 'there will be too much Mage Eras in DE 2 to have Arthurian one being Mage also' - I want to recall everyone that Kickstarter started with two Eras from Vampire ( French Revolution and 1001 Nights ) - with Steamboats rather winning ( and being connected to New Orleans ) I think we will have 3 Vampires Era till this date.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T10:32:34-07:00","id":1121946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1121927#post1121927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or it would be leaving those hooks in place for people to use they want and build brand new hooks for two other gamelines that can work alongside them.<br /> <br /> Look, I'm not disagreeing that it probably will be Mage or saying that I don't want it to be. I'm just saying that there are other options and that nothing is a given at this point. I can see Arthurian Eras that are Mummy/Vampire, Werewolf/Changeling, Promethean/Hunter, Demon/Beast, and more variations that could be successful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are few eras besides Arthur that could be called as instrumental to the development of the tropes of many different splats. The time is a mystery, as well. Anything could go, could be made to fit. My hope is that they strongly develop the side-material indicating what is happening for related parts of the CofD in this era in particular.<br /> <br /> If they fail to do that it will be disappointing, but I'm confident the community will rise to the occasion and fill in holes.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 07-28-2017, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T10:56:21-07:00","id":1121961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1121946#post1121946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are few eras besides Arthur that could be called as instrumental to the development of the tropes of many different splats. The time is a mystery, as well. Anything could go, could be made to fit. My hope is that they strongly develop the side-material indicating when is happening for related parts of the CofD in this era in particular.<br /> <br /> If they fail to do that it will be disappointing, but I'm confident the community will rise to the occasion and fill in holes.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly confident that they will. Those sidebars were super popular last time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T12:14:58-07:00","id":1121992,"title":"","content":"Mage/Hunter would be awesome. Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T12:16:47-07:00","id":1121994,"title":"","content":"The Knights of the round establish and follow a Code. And it's not as if compacts controlled or formed by mages are unheard of.<br /> <br /> People may not think about werewolf immediately when they come across World War 1, but some of the first lines from Werewolf the Forsaken are, 'Werewolf is a game of savage violence and bloody horror.' 'Werewolf is about dominance and violence, about a world divided into &quot;us&quot; and &quot;them.&quot; It's about hunting and being hunted in turn. It's about how far you would go for one of your own.' Which fits World War 1, and many other wars, quite nicely.<br /> <br /> Dark Eras don't always go for the 'easy' way. Doubting Souls was a time of witch burnings, that would have fit Mage just as well as it did Hunter. After the Fall had a large section on Dracula, but was a Demon chapter. Second Sight could have gone to mages. Aztec period for vampires. And so on.<br /> <br /> I'm sure Mage will be one of the eras but I wouldn't be aghast at the thought of them going another direction. They could just have a section detailing Merlin as a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-28-2017, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T16:31:34-07:00","id":1122124,"title":"","content":"The fact that no one knows who Arthur was shouts Demon Legend to me. It was a circle trying to forge a Hell through a partnership with Merlin... who screwed them when he Ascended. But the reality is that <i>all</i> the possible Arthurs <i>were</i> Arthur. Most of them were Covers, and they all shared the Legend.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really work thematically until you start pulling in the clash of religions/civilizations, so that there's actual room for espionage activity to occur. It's easy to pose the G-M as arriving through missionaries of Christianity, but it's more interesting to frame L'Morte of Arthur as the G-M co-opting druidism to create Mordred as a new kind of hunter-angel. But that's the limit of my knowledge of Descent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T17:06:06-07:00","id":1122135,"title":"","content":"*comes in to fight for Mage/Hunter*<br /> <br /> *someone already did that*<br /> <br /> *goes back to study*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T22:15:38-07:00","id":1122227,"title":"","content":"I'm semi-hyped for Arthurian Mage/Hunter - finally my fan Legacy <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/92189-european-knight-legacy?p=95253#post95253\">Order of Round Table</a> would come from Hunter Compact working under Merlin! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T01:33:41-07:00","id":1122263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1122227#post1122227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm semi-hyped for Arthurian Mage/Hunter - finally my fan Legacy <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/92189-european-knight-legacy?p=95253#post95253\">Order of Round Table</a> would come from Hunter Compact working under Merlin! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I think about it, Mage/Hunter could be a good alternative to Mage/Changeling (or perhaps we could have all three with expansion, if we're lucky). The Knights of the Round Table keeping the land secure against monstrous threats does fit the era. And whether or not would the knights as Hunters have supernatural abilities that would make them Sleepwalkers could be made irrelevant if they were also a line of Proximi, perhaps made by drinking from the Grail. Or maybe each would be a different Proximus, giving each of the legendary knights a unique set of abilities distinguishing them from each other. Or perhaps only Arthur is a Proximus, with the knights being Hunters with Supernatural abilities. The era could mention multiple alternatives (many Arthurs after all) and the ability to make Proximi would make the Grail a truly legendary item.<br /> <br /> I'm not certain if you can have Hunters who are Proximi, it might be mixing splats, but than again, Hunters <i>are</i> still mortal humans. Besides, a Mage/Hunter crossover where you have two groups with such different power and yet both of them are essentially the most human splats in their nature could lead to interesting storytelling opportunities, especially if they are allied against common threats.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To add Mage story hooks, we know that Ruin threw a hissy fit about the very existence of Camelot and tried to completely obliterate it, which it failed to do. But whenever an &quot;Arthur&quot; surfaces and tries to create a new Camelot, I can imagine Ruin attempting to eliminate him as soon as possible. Efforts of Cabals in this era could be about preventing the destruction of everything they hold dear by covert powerful supernatural forces and their villainous (proto)Seer minions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 07-29-2017, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T10:56:16-07:00","id":1123552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1122263#post1122263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think about it, Mage/Hunter could be a good alternative to Mage/Changeling (or perhaps we could have all three with expansion, if we're lucky). The Knights of the Round Table keeping the land secure against monstrous threats does fit the era. And whether or not would the knights as Hunters have supernatural abilities that would make them Sleepwalkers could be made irrelevant if they were also a line of Proximi, perhaps made by drinking from the Grail. Or maybe each would be a different Proximus, giving each of the legendary knights a unique set of abilities distinguishing them from each other. Or perhaps only Arthur is a Proximus, with the knights being Hunters with Supernatural abilities. The era could mention multiple alternatives (many Arthurs after all) and the ability to make Proximi would make the Grail a truly legendary item.<br /> <br /> I'm not certain if you can have Hunters who are Proximi, it might be mixing splats, but than again, Hunters <i>are</i> still mortal humans. Besides, a Mage/Hunter crossover where you have two groups with such different power and yet both of them are essentially the most human splats in their nature could lead to interesting storytelling opportunities, especially if they are allied against common threats.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To add Mage story hooks, we know that Ruin threw a hissy fit about the very existence of Camelot and tried to completely obliterate it, which it failed to do. But whenever an &quot;Arthur&quot; surfaces and tries to create a new Camelot, I can imagine Ruin attempting to eliminate him as soon as possible. Efforts of Cabals in this era could be about preventing the destruction of everything they hold dear by covert powerful supernatural forces and their villainous (proto)Seer minions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd buy it. <br /> <br /> The idea that the Grail creates Proximi from those whom it permits to drink (only incidentally healing them) is hereby &quot;borrowed&quot;. I do adore elegance.<br /> <br /> Would you be willing to expand a bit on your comments regarding Ruin and what it and/or the Seers could do against the original Camelot? I mean, they *could* act, since Supernal Time-sight would or could enable observation that Merlin was going to ascend... maybe... or not?!<br /> <br /> The core problem as I understood it was that Ruin and/or Prophet obliterated Camelot through a Working of Imperium in response to Merlin's ascension; however since Merlin had already ascended--a Supernal Truth--they could not utterly obliterate his trace in much the same way that they cannot obliterate &quot;Atlantis&quot; as it underpins their very existence in the (mutilated) timeline. This has always struck me as a sequence that, if lived through, would look rather linear: live through Camelot and Merlin, Arthur dies, everything goes to crap with rampaging Saxons and people quickly just forgetting everything of the time before... stonemasons and smiths die and their previous works are lost, rust or whatnot; castles are torn down and their stones reused or lost, and even the oral traditions are forgotten as people's memories fade or those who know the stories meet with accidents. <br /> <br /> Atomic destruction via Fate, in other words.<br /> <br /> Also: were not the Seers extant at this time? What did the Exarchs use as minions if not the Iron Pyramid?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T11:23:57-07:00","id":1123564,"title":"","content":"Less organized groups of mages and cults. The Seers were originally factions in the same organizations that would eventually become the Diamond Orders.<br /> <br /> I have to imagine there were still independents back then, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-01-2017, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T11:38:12-07:00","id":1123572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1123552#post1123552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd buy it.<br /> <br /> The idea that the Grail creates Proximi from those whom it permits to drink (only incidentally healing them) is hereby &quot;borrowed&quot;. I do adore elegance.<br /> <br /> Would you be willing to expand a bit on your comments regarding Ruin and what it and/or the Seers could do against the original Camelot? I mean, they *could* act, since Supernal Time-sight would or could enable observation that Merlin was going to ascend... maybe... or not?!<br /> <br /> The core problem as I understood it was that Ruin and/or Prophet obliterated Camelot through a Working of Imperium in response to Merlin's ascension; however since Merlin had already ascended--a Supernal Truth--they could not utterly obliterate his trace in much the same way that they cannot obliterate &quot;Atlantis&quot; as it underpins their very existence in the (mutilated) timeline. This has always struck me as a sequence that, if lived through, would look rather linear: live through Camelot and Merlin, Arthur dies, everything goes to crap with rampaging Saxons and people quickly just forgetting everything of the time before... stonemasons and smiths die and their previous works are lost, rust or whatnot; castles are torn down and their stones reused or lost, and even the oral traditions are forgotten as people's memories fade or those who know the stories meet with accidents.<br /> <br /> Atomic destruction via Fate, in other words.<br /> <br /> Also: were not the Seers extant at this time? What did the Exarchs use as minions if not the Iron Pyramid?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I guess that the Seers were already extant as they had enough time to develop from the Tyrannoi and I believe the GotV book mentions them as well with them existing during the times of the Roman Empire. Ministries, on the other hand, existed only since the renaissance, so those would be out.<br /> <br /> Regarding Ruin, I was acually talking about the situation, where Camelot was already destroyed and Merlin Ascended, but I was considering the effect of symbolism created by Merlin's Ascension. If all this stuff regarding the legend is a part of Merlin's personal symbolism, then Camelot and Arthur basically still exist in the Supernal and just like other symbols (like Atlantean symbolism through repeatedly aggreating mages into the Diamond orders) will work to create this kind of repeating event, where a guy (using a Shadow Name Arthur) tries to create a perfect kingdom. The Ruin cannot eliminate these events completely, but will obviously try to destroy these manifestations, whenever and wherever they arise, since they are a direct threat to its own symbolism.<br /> <br /> Also, considering the omnipresent Fate and Time shenanigans, an interesting idea is that of contemporary mages travelling to the past and dealing with all this stuff. Maybe an Emanation might connect you to the past and you could use it to go back in time to deal with the previously described manifestations. You probably couldn't travel to <i>the</i> Camelot, since, like Atlantis, it didn't technically exist in this timeline. On the other hand, maybe the idea of the true Camelot, as Supernal in nature thanks to Merlin, is actually timeless and present in the aforementioned Emanation, with the Emanation having irises to different eras on the real timeline, while staying there allows you to interact with the many mythical versions of Camelot, Arthur and Merlin (Emanations being filled with humanity's mythology and becoming more pure the closer you get to the entrance into the Supernal is in fact described in the 2E entry on Emanations).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T12:05:26-07:00","id":1123588,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> mentioned few times before that United Kingdom mages used term 'Camelot' to describe phenomena known on Mediterranean Sea as 'Atlantis' - and ( from, I suppose Age of Exploration onward ) called generally 'Time Before'. ( I added Age of Exploration as 'Atlantis' timelessness is called different names across the globe and till Age of Exploration, you do not truly need to contrast those varies names, because local mages get what you mean about 'Camelot', 'Mu' or 'Atlantis' ).<br /> <br /> Dave wanted to used whole 'Merlin shananigans' for his <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Anarchy\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchy Era</a> previously, with last pre-Mysterium merging of Panscryptias and Keepers of the Word would fight over the scraps of 'Camelots' Artifact - and giving proper write-up for the two Orders. As Arthurian Britain took place Anarchy Era - <b>Are we going to Panscryptias and Keepers write-ups?</b> In the end, Arthurian Era is on the other side of timeline, with Merlin time changes being 'just second away'.<br /> <br /> And Seers in that time are already an Order ( they are from start of Roman Empire ), they are just much more coalitions of 'Order Caucuses', just like any Diamond Order is in that time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-01-2017, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T00:25:45-07:00","id":1139121,"title":"","content":"Reading now Polish historical magazine article about Arthurian Legends, they point that name Arthur may come from Roman nickname 'Artos' that mean Bear. So it could easily be just nickname for some Roman - or Roman-descending - general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T04:46:55-07:00","id":1139144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1139121#post1139121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading now Polish historical magazine article about Arthurian Legends, they point that name Arthur may come from Roman nickname 'Artos' that mean Bear. So it could easily be just nickname for some Roman - or Roman-descending - general.</div> </div> </div> </div>They seem to have confused things a bit. Artos doesn't mean Bear as far as I can find out, though there seems to be a popular etymology for Arthur that it comes in part from a Brittonic word for Bear.<br /> <br /> Also Arctos (as in the character from Mage) means Bear in Ancient Greek.<br /> <br /> Hey, I only just noticed that the spiritual descendant of Merlin called his apprentice Arctos... I see what he did there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T06:56:59-07:00","id":1139170,"title":"","content":"In magazine, they pointed that whole 'Artos' thing is from old Celtic, not Latin, sorry for confusion here. It's even name based for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artio\" target=\"_blank\">Artio Celtic goddess</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T10:31:41-07:00","id":1146721,"title":"","content":"One of my players send my interesting video on the topic of early Dark Ages Britain politics - describing the time future Dark Era is suppose to take on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jHNdQW4eMTM\" data-code=\"jHNdQW4eMTM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/jHNdQW4eMTM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T12:34:34-07:00","id":1150729,"title":"","content":"So I can finally say this: <br /> <br /> Arthurian Britannia will be a Vampire/Changeling/Hunter era. God damn that feels good!<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T12:44:05-07:00","id":1150734,"title":"","content":"I like the addition of Vampire.<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see how they'll swing it, really. Will the Knights be Hunters, Vampires, or Changelings? All three? Two? Apparently the gamelines aren't meant to conflict, so it wouldn't just be Vampire versus Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T23:23:23-07:00","id":1150911,"title":"","content":"My take: Changeling is a ready fit and Vampire\u2019s established history ties in very well. If anything, I\u2019m cocking my head at Hunter\u2019s inclusion in this, unless we\u2019re going to see whatever shape the Knights of Saint George took before they were Anglican. Am I missing something here?<br /> <br /> As for Mage, what we want from the setting is almost completely divorced from the actual history of the time. I would sooner see an Arthurian Mage as its own wild, weird thing rather than one under the constraints of historicity and crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T00:12:40-07:00","id":1150917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1150911#post1150911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything, I\u2019m cocking my head at Hunter\u2019s inclusion in this, unless we\u2019re going to see whatever shape the Knights of Saint George took before they were Anglican. Am I missing something here?</div> </div> </div> </div>That since we got samurai hunters in Fallen Blossoms, now is the time for knight hunters? I guess?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T03:28:53-07:00","id":1150943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1150917#post1150917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That since we got samurai hunters in Fallen Blossoms, now is the time for knight hunters? I guess?</div> </div> </div> </div>actually, we didn't really got them- the Gimu were cut out in the finale product (even though they are still available online, like the Cursed of Hachiku which were cut from Hurt Locker)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T04:46:28-07:00","id":1150953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1150911#post1150911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take: Changeling is a ready fit and Vampire\u2019s established history ties in very well. If anything, I\u2019m cocking my head at Hunter\u2019s inclusion in this, unless we\u2019re going to see whatever shape the Knights of Saint George took before they were Anglican. Am I missing something here?<br /> <br /> As for Mage, what we want from the setting is almost completely divorced from the actual history of the time. I would sooner see an Arthurian Mage as its own wild, weird thing rather than one under the constraints of historicity and crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Knights of the Round Table as a Hunter Conspiracy, maybe one that hunts True Fae and Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T06:03:49-07:00","id":1150970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1150943#post1150943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">actually, we didn't really got them- the Gimu were cut out in the finale product (even though they are still available online, like the Cursed of Hachiku which were cut from Hurt Locker)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooh. Interesting. I didn't know there was cut sections in those books. Do you have the links? Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 10-19-2017, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T08:09:35-07:00","id":1151012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1150970#post1150970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooooh. Interesting. I didn't know there was cut sections in those books. Do you have the links? Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly &quot;cut section&quot; as much as ideas presented in the Open Development which didn't got to the finale book. The Cursed show up in <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GE8UBd43fIYUZ-jNC_cAx_7if_-2d6bX_iaygAJYZ28/edit\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, while the Gimu are <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1UkJgf3IjdQuKvHmX_OxL6uBjCt02go-knYZ0Pc_UMVE/edit#heading=h.cg4hapvd9kbx\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T08:19:47-07:00","id":1151016,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on the selected lines: <br /> <br /> Changeling is a no-brainer to me. Lady of the Lake as a True Fae, Avalon as a realm in Arcadia, etc. Possibly some foreshadowing of that plot hook in Requiem for Regina about the deal the London Kindred made with the True Fae. Plus, being set in the British Isles gives an opportunity to explore the fact that a lot of Anglo-Celtic folklore pertains to fairies. <br /> <br /> Hunter surprised me at first, but the interpretation that the KotRT were a Hunter compact fighting monsters is too good to pass up. <br /> <br /> Vampire has me wondering if we will see an update of the Bron bloodline, since their backstory is tied very closely to the Grail Mythos, which plays a part in Arthurian legend, and the fact that Grail legends mix a lot of Christian tradition and Celtic mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T16:42:28-07:00","id":1154252,"title":"","content":"So, thinking about the Vampire side of the setting, will we see the Weyhan Cynn's origin? Perhaps more in touch with the stryx? What about it's rival cult, the Fuil-Beannaithe? I hope there is a write-up for them. But I imagine they're more like the Circle of the Crone.<br /> <br /> The Invictus wouldn't exist already and the Lancea et Sanctum will be very strong. Also, we will probably see the Legion of the Dead in it's post-Rome, pre-Gallows state.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T18:31:23-07:00","id":1154270,"title":"","content":"As someone who has read literally hundreds of books of Arthuriana (original chronicles, original telling and retelling, studies both literary and historical, modern reimaginings, scholarly and non-scholarly articles, New Age interpretations, etc.), I have always approached the &quot;historical King Arthur&quot; very warily. He has been sighted anywhere between the late 2nd century and the early 9th, in Britain (many locales), Wales, Scotland, Brittany, and Eastern Europe. His name has been tied to an ancient word meaning &quot;king/royal&quot;, to a twisted version of the word &quot;bear&quot;, several ancient gods and goddesses, most of those with little known about them, and even an early corruption of &quot;Christ&quot;. His court grows, shrinks, and moves about randomly. No one even agrees on what tales are absolutely core to the canon and which are not.<br /> <br /> For all this, I love my Mabinogian, my Le Notre D'Arthur, my Once &amp; Future King. I love my Gwalchmai as much as my Gawain, and my Bedwyr as much as my Bedivere. And, yes, I love Monty Python and the Holy Trail. <br /> <br /> Whatever comes out of this exercise will be in no wise the &quot;real Arthur&quot;; I've given up looking for him. But I will probably be slightly amused by whatever is cooked up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T10:20:24-08:00","id":1157311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1150729#post1150729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I can finally say this:<br /> <br /> Arthurian Britannia will be a Vampire/Changeling/Hunter era. God damn that feels good!<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I approve. This takes Merlin from being &quot;that mage dude we hang with sometimes&quot; and keeps him firmly as an esoteric dressing character.<br /> <br /> I'm going to guess that there are knightly hunter groups that ... hunt... adventuresome beasts. Questing... beasts. Ehem. <br /> <br /> Did they define the year-spread yet? That's kinda important, otherwise.<br /> <br /> Otherwise? I'm expecting a bit more on the Weyhan Cynn, Fuil-Beannaithe (I picture these as a kind of split between British and Irish Druidism--which were different) and of course the Legion of the Dead/Gallows Post. (As Max Deltree commented.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T18:33:28-08:00","id":1157670,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it's at all possible to include a Promethean interpretation of the Fisher King legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T19:00:40-08:00","id":1157674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1157670#post1157670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it's at all possible to include a Promethean interpretation of the Fisher King legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did play with that idea for an expansion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T21:11:47-08:00","id":1157692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1157670#post1157670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it's at all possible to include a Promethean interpretation of the Fisher King legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literary one of main motives the Soulless and Dead ( Black Death) Dark Era is based on...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T10:54:13-08:00","id":1157783,"title":"","content":"Cool to hear.<br /> <br /> I remember reading somewhere (probably a review of the Clive Owen Arthur firm that came out last decade) that the Arthurian legend has always adapted to fit the needs of different generations, resulting in it being so diverse and at times flexible. As such, it would probably be easy to do an entire Dark Eras book about it, with each supernatural getting its own interpretation of the mythos, picking which parts fit best with each game's themes. Werewolf as a gritty historical conflict between Celtic British and Saxon invaders, Hunter doing the Round Table as a Conspiracy, Beast turning the whole thing on its head with dragons, witches and giants being tormented by Heroic knights, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T22:06:07-07:00","id":1211691,"title":"","content":"Relevant to this thread, but <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-2/posts/2171940\" target=\"_blank\">latest monthly KS update focuses on the Arthurian Dark Era. </a><br /> <br /> Highlights include:<br /> <br /> -Confirmation (if they didn't already) on the Bron bloodline getting included and receiving a 2e update.<br /> <br /> -Mentions on some of the nonfiction sources of inspiration.<br /> <br /> -The themes and mood:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The themes in this era are:<br /> <br /> <b>Change:</b> For all three creature types present in this era, the times, they are a-changin\u2019. Vampires do not desire this change, the Lost are split between change and former glories, while the hunters proudly instigate this change. Can the three work together to make something acceptable for all involved, or are all destined for their own brand of ruin?<br /> <br /> <b>Darkness:</b> In what will later become known as the Dark Ages, Britain is about to enter the era of warring kings and barons, persecution of scholars, and end to freedom of trade. While Britain was not sleeping at this time, life under the Saxons was wholly different to life under the Romans (for better and worse). For the established nobility, this was a time of encroaching darkness.<br /> <br /> The mood for this era is:<br /> <br /> <b>Gloom:</b> The world is growing smaller, the nights are drawing in, the invaders are coming, and blood flows readily. The glory that was Rome has faded. Gloom has overtaken King Arthur\u2019s Britannia. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T04:49:20-07:00","id":1212225,"title":"","content":"Can any one give me an idea what the Bron bloodline is and what its connection to Grail is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:49:49-07:00","id":1212274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1212225#post1212225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can any one give me an idea what the Bron bloodline is and what its connection to Grail is?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I remember the Bron bloodline, are a Circle/Sanctum bloodline whose members are all on a quest for the Holy Grail, whether that's the Grail of Christ or the Cealtic mythic Grail/Mead pot depends on the members. I think the reason they are searching for it is because of there bloodline weakness, tho I forget. It's been a long time since I read so details are fuzzy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T16:37:42-07:00","id":1212490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120287-de2-arthurian-discussion?p=1212274#post1212274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I remember the Bron bloodline, are a Circle/Sanctum bloodline whose members are all on a quest for the Holy Grail, whether that's the Grail of Christ or the Cealtic mythic Grail/Mead pot depends on the members. I think the reason they are searching for it is because of there bloodline weakness, tho I forget. It's been a long time since I read so details are fuzzy</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh thank you, that sounds cool. Maybe the Knights of the Round table will be Vampires. That would be very different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T08:52:44-07:00","id":1343995,"title":"","content":"Great (and sarcastic ) analysis of Arthurian myths in social context they were created. From Roman general war stories to christian courtly love drama. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, how those stories were more and more saturated with with Christian but ALSO Celtic elements in each new iterations. Good video!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i_jgF-S746o\" data-code=\"i_jgF-S746o\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/i_jgF-S746o/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}